  "notes": "{鈍化|どんか} refers to the process of becoming slower or less vigorous, primarily used in economic and business contexts.\n\nWRITING:\n- {鈍|どん} (dull, blunt, slow)\n- {化|か} (-ification, becoming)\n\nUSAGE:\n- {鈍化|どんか}する (to slow down, to decelerate - suru verb)\n- 〜の{鈍化|どんか} (slowdown of ~)\n\nCOMMON SUBJECTS:\n- {経済|けいざい}{成長|せいちょう}の{鈍化|どんか} (economic growth slowdown)\n- {景気|けいき}の{鈍化|どんか} (economic slowdown)\n- {消費|しょうひ}の{鈍化|どんか} (consumption slowdown)\n- {需要|じゅよう}の{鈍化|どんか} (demand deceleration)\n- インフレの{鈍化|どんか} (inflation slowdown)\n\nREGISTER:\n- Formal/technical\n- Common in economic news, business reports, and financial analysis\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {加速|かそく} (acceleration) - opposite\n- {停滞|ていたい} (stagnation) - more severe than {鈍化|どんか}\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {減速|げんそく} (deceleration, slowdown)\n- {停滞|ていたい} (stagnation)\n- {低迷|ていめい} (sluggishness, slump)\n- {下降|かこう} (decline, downturn)",
